    "method": "Four exact cleared published Qualla daytimePD-selforiginals and original two-wing native plan inspected; comparative local native plan plotted/inspected.",
    "notes": "Four exact published native QuallaPD-selforiginals inspected. Regani2272x1704west-wing view shows pale/grey coursed coral stone, rounded south end, tall pale green projecting shuttered oriels with sloped red-brown hoods/brackets, small pointed lights, stepped battering buttress feet, open pointed gallery, corbelled cornice and four-faced black/gold clock on the square battlement/pinnacle tower. Two640x480CaribDigitaeast-wing views show long open upper pointed arcade/green balustrade, lower round arcade, projecting courtyard-facing pointed/gabled entrance block, low hipped roofs and rounded far end. KevinGabbert2000x1500published photograph shows matching green iron front rails/gates and west gallery/gabled entry/tower; tree obstruction/hidden detail is not copied. Original native footprints retain both separate wings and actual rounded/faceted ends; no native roof heights or separate tower polygon exists, so roof sections/tower placement within the west projection and small concealed details are bounded estimates. No supplemental imagery or photo texture used."
  },
